  "question": {
    "text": "A ball is dropped from the top of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> high tower on a planet. In the last <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> before hitting the ground, it covers a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Acceleration due to gravity (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) near the surface on that planet is______",
